  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "A drone has positive velocity $v(t)$ after being flown upward from an initial height of $0$ feet at time  $t=0$ seconds. The velocity of the drone is recorded for selected values of $t$ over the interval $0\\le t\\le 40$ seconds, as shown in the table below. \n\n| $t\\,\\text{(seconds)}$ | $0$ | $7$ | $15$ | $25$ | $32$ | $40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v\\,\\text{(feet/second)}$ | $3$ | $10$ | $25$ | $40$ | $46$ | $49$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum over $[0,40]$ with five subintervals to approximate the total distance covered by the drone.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the velocity-time graph.*",
